.TH qsh-mcp 1  "mcp 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-mcp \- Serve MCP tools over stdio (`docs/CLI.md` §8). Not an operation: no envelope, nothing on stdout but JSON\-RPC frames — every diagnostic goes to stderr, exactly like `qsh serve`/`qsh listen`/`qsh reverse` (`docs/CLI.md` §8.1, §2.2). No flags: MVP is stdio\-only
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh mcp\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Serve MCP tools over stdio (`docs/CLI.md` §8). Not an operation: no envelope, nothing on stdout but JSON\-RPC frames — every diagnostic goes to stderr, exactly like `qsh serve`/`qsh listen`/`qsh reverse` (`docs/CLI.md` §8.1, §2.2). No flags: MVP is stdio\-only
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
